{title: 521 - Depth of Mercy}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #521 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 521}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Depth of [C]mercy!—can there [F]be
Mercy [C]still re[C7]served for [F]me?
[Bb]Can my [F]God His [C]wrath [G7]for[C]bear?
[F]Me, the [C]chief of sinners, [F]spare?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]I have [C]long withstood [F]His grace,
[C]Long provoked [C7]Him to [F]His face,
[Bb]Would [F]not [C]hearken [G7]to [C]His calls,
[F]Grieved Him [C]by a [F]thousand falls.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Now [C]incline me [F]to repent;
[C]Let me [C7]now my [F]sins lament;
[Bb]Now [F]my [C]foul [G7]revolt [C]deplore,
[F]Weep, believe, [C]and sin [F]no more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]There for [C]me the [F]Savior stands,
[C]Shows His [C7]wounds and [F]spreads His hands;
[Bb]God [F]is [C]love! I [G7]know, [C]I feel;
[F]Jesus weeps, [C]and loves [F]me still.
{end_of_verse}
